This file contains some important hints for translators.


The current status of the Clay translation can be checked at

  https://l10n.gnome.org/module/clay


Translation of the GNU Image Manipulation Program is handled by the
GNOME Translation Project (see https://l10n.gnome.org/). If you want to
help, we suggest that you get in touch with the translation team of
your language (see https://l10n.gnome.org/teams/).


Clay is different

 Clay is a complex application which has a bunch of scripts and
 plug-ins that all want to be internationalized. Therefore there is
 not one catalog but many. For a full translation of Clay's UI, you
 will have to add translations for the following catalogs:

   po/clay30.pot                                      --  the core
   po-libclay/clay30-libclay.pot                      --  the libclay library
   po-plugins/clay30-std-plugins.pot                  --  the C plug-ins
   po-python/clay30-python.pot                        --  the pyclay plug-ins
   po-script-fu/clay30-script-fu.pot                  --  the script-fu scripts
   po-tips/clay30-tips.pot                            --  the startup tips
   po-windows-installer/clay30-windows-installer.pot  --  the windows installer

 If you are looking for the translations of clay-perl, please note that
 clay-perl has been moved into it's own git module called
 clay-perl.


Clay Tips dialog

 In addition to message catalogs Clay provides a file with tips that
 are displayed in the Tips dialog. This file is in XML format and can
 be found in the tips directory. The english tips messages are
 extracted from clay-tips.xml.in so translators can use the usual
 tools to create a <lang>.po file that holds the translations. All
 translations are then merged into clay-tips.xml with language
 identifiers taken from the po filename.

 Clay needs to know what language it should select from clay-tips.xml.
 Therefore, there's the special message "tips-locale:C" in the main
 message catalog that needs to be translated correctly. For a german
 translation of the tips this would look like this:

 #: ../app/dialogs/tips-parser.c:188
 msgid "tips-locale:C"
 msgstr "tips-locale:de"


Localization of third-party plug-ins

 Third-party plug-ins (plug-ins that are not distributed with Clay)
 can't have their messages in the clay-std-plugins textdomain.  We
 have therefore provided a mechanism that allows plug-ins to install
 their own message catalogs and tell Clay to bind to that
 textdomain. This is necessary so that Clay can correctly translate
 the menu paths the plug-in registers. Basically the plug-in has to
 call clay_plugin_domain_add() or clay_domain_plugin_add_with_path()
 before it registers any functions. Have a look at the script-fu
 plug-in to see how this is done in detail.
